      "amount": "2 tbsp",
      "notes": "chopped for garnish"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat.",
    "Add the chopped onion and minced garlic and sauté until fragrant and translucent.",
    "Stir in the sliced carrot and celery and cook for 3 minutes.",
    "Add the chestnut mushrooms and confit tomatoes and cook until the mushrooms soften, about 5 minutes.",
    "Pour in the vegetable broth and bring the mixture to a gentle boil.",
    "Reduce the heat to low, add thyme, bay leaf, salt, and pepper, and simmer uncovered for 25 minutes.",
    "Remove the bay leaf and let the stew cool for a few minutes before transferring it into mason jars.",
    "Garnish each jar with chopped fresh parsley.",
    "Cover and refrigerate; reheat gently before serving."
  ],
